msgid "葛城の山々は、山で心と体をきたえる「修験道（しゅげんどう）」のはじまりの地といわれます。役行者（えんのぎょうじゃ）が、お経を納めたと伝わる場所が「経塚（きょうづか）」です。経塚は、お経の28の章にあたる28番まであり、3つの番号には2か所ずつあるので、全部で31か所です。"
msgstr "The Katsuragi mountains are said to be where Shugendo began, a practice of training mind and body in the mountains. The places where En no Gyoja is said to have buried sutras are called kyozuka (sutra mounds). They are numbered 1 to 28, after the 28 chapters of the sutra, and three of the numbers have two places each, so there are 31 in all."

